Onderzoekers kijken naar de toepasbaarheid van het stakeholderraamwerk van Mitchell, Agle en Wood  (MAW)\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardeftab720\ri-2769\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Through 57 key informant interviews and policy reviews, the authors categorize stakeholders into "latent," "expectant," and "definitive" groups. The study concludes that while politicians are often the most "salient" (definitive) stakeholders, the framework provides a superior tool for identifying "dangerous" or "dependent" stakeholders who might otherwise be overlooked in traditional power-interest grids. This source is highly relevant for researchers in health policy, public administration, and organizational management.\
\
\ul Theoretisch uitgangspunt\
\ulnone Het model van MAW gaat uit van 3 klassen stakeholders. De indeling is gebaseerd op drie kenmerken (die ik nu ook gebruik):\
1. Latent\
	- \
2. Expectant\
3. Definitive \
\

